.TH ZGCTL 1 "September 2026" "snd-zg01-tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zgctl \- control the Yamaha ZG01 audio interface driver
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zgctl
.RB [ \-c
.IR card ]
.B list
.br
.B zgctl
.RB [ \-c
.IR card ]
.B get
.IR CONTROL
.br
.B zgctl
.RB [ \-c
.IR card ]
.B set
.IR CONTROL
.IR VALUE
.br
.B zgctl
.RB [ \-c
.IR card ]
.B save
.br
.B zgctl
.RB [ \-c
.IR card ]
.B reset
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zgctl
lists and changes the mixer controls that the
.B snd-zg01
driver exposes for the Yamaha ZG01 USB audio interface: the microphone
GATE, compressor, equalizer and limiter, plus saving and reloading the
device settings.
.PP
It talks to the ALSA control device directly and needs no libasound.
.PP
The card is found automatically by its driver name
.RB ( zg01_usb ).
Use
.B \-c
to select another card by id or driver name.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List every control with its current value.
.TP
.BI get " CONTROL"
Print one control.
.TP
.BI set " CONTROL VALUE"
Write one control.
.TP
.B save
Persist the current settings to the device's non-volatile memory
(the
.RB \(lq Save to ZG01 \(rq
control).
.TP
.B reset
Reload the persisted settings, dropping unsaved changes
(the
.RB \(lq Reset to ZG01 \(rq
control).
.SH VALUES
.TP
.B Gains
In dB, for example
.BR +6.0 " or " \-3.5 .
.TP
.B Frequencies
In Hz, with
.B k
or
.B kHz
suffixes, for example
.BR 1k " or " 7.5kHz .
.TP
.B Q
As a ratio, for example
.BR 2.0 .
.TP
.B Switches
.BR on " or " off .
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
zgctl list
zgctl get 'EQ Band 1 Gain'
zgctl set 'EQ Band 1 Gain' +6.0
zgctl set 'EQ Band 2 Frequency' 1k
zgctl set 'Limiter Capture Switch' on
zgctl save
.fi
.SH NOTES
Values read back are the last value the driver wrote, not a read from the
device (the device exposes no usable per-parameter read).  Settings
changed outside the driver are not reflected until written again.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR amixer (1),
.BR alsamixer (1)
